Only the radeon driver uses the <drm/drm_pciids.h> header. Instead of
defining a macro there and use it (also) only once, remove one
indirection and put the numbers directly into the pci_device_id array.

Signed-off-by: Uwe Kleine-König (The Capable Hub) <u.kleine-koenig@baylibre.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_drv.c | 702 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/drm/drm_pciids.h            | 702 ----------------------------
 2 files changed, 700 insertions(+), 704 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 include/drm/drm_pciids.h

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_drv.c
